# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
#
# Pinned configuration for the OSU Micro-Benchmarks dogfooding target (Stage 7,
# MPI compiler wrapper). The OSU Micro-Benchmarks build with mpicc/mpicxx, the
# Open MPI compiler wrappers. mpicc is a REAL wrapper binary (opal_wrapper) that
# execs gcc with the MPI include/library flags spliced in, so Bear intercepts
# BOTH the mpicc invocation and the gcc child it spawns. This target validates,
# in a real LD_PRELOAD build, two decisions the integration tests can only
# simulate: that Bear records the mpicc command verbatim (wrapper-verbatim), and
# that the driver+child pair collapses to a SINGLE entry per translation unit
# (no true duplicate). A dogfooding configuration is (base image digest, target
# source revision, target build type); all are pinned (dogfood-pinned-target).
# Sourced by run.sh; SRC_DIR is also consumed by the target Containerfile via
# podman build --build-arg.

# Validation mode for this target: 'none'. OSU has no committed golden and no
# CMake oracle (it uses autotools), so it is run ONLY with the target-agnostic
# on-demand checks. Per the Stage 7 plan the meaningful ones here are
# --invariants (its no-true-duplicates clause is exactly the driver+child
# collapse assertion), --determinism (two builds equivalent), and --replay (the
# recorded mpicc command re-accepts -fsyntax-only, since mpicc forwards it to
# gcc). run.sh dispatches on this selector.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
VALIDATION="none"

# Pinned base image: the same digest zlib/curl/ffmpeg use (this IS fedora:44,
# the devcontainer base). An unpinned base would let a package update change the
# compiler or the Open MPI version under the fixed checks and produce phantom
# diffs.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
BASE_IMAGE="registry.fedoraproject.org/fedora@sha256:3baf5f0dededfd939eb8f0b271ff8ad17bdb381cdd5768bd7d6f45bba795aa62"

# Fixed in-container build path (dogfood-fixed-paths). OSU builds IN-TREE:
# objects land next to their sources under /src (autotools supports VPATH, but
# an in-tree build keeps this target as simple as ffmpeg's), so source, objects,
# and build dir are all this one fixed path. A fixed path keeps absolute paths
# in 'directory' reproducible across runs (so determinism needs no
# normalization).
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
SRC_DIR="/src"

# Object-count instrument for the entry-count invariant (dogfood-invariants).
# OSU's automake build compiles each benchmark source exactly once and leaves
# the object on disk under /src, so the DEFAULT instrument, a post-build
# `find $OBJECTS_DIR -name '*.o' | wc -l`, is the right cross-check: it must
# equal Bear's entry count, which it does only if the driver+child collapse left
# ONE entry per object (a failed collapse would roughly double Bear's count
# against a fixed object count - the check the no-true-duplicates invariant and
# this band both guard). OSU therefore does NOT override OBJECT_COUNT_CMD.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
OBJECTS_DIR="/src"

# Build directory passed to the replay sampler (dogfood-replay) as
# `cdb-compare sample --build-dir`. OSU builds in-tree, so its build dir IS
# /src.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
BUILD_DIR="/src"

# Tolerance percent for the entry-count band
# (--expected-objects N --tolerance OBJECT_TOLERANCE_PCT). OSU compiles each
# source once and leaves the object on disk, so `find` tracks Bear's entry count
# tightly; 10% absorbs an incidental configure-probe object across OSU releases
# without a false fail.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
OBJECT_TOLERANCE_PCT="10"

# Per-target preflight minimum free disk on the podman graphroot, in KiB
# (dogfood-preflight). OSU is small (a few hundred objects), but the base +
# target images still dominate; ~4 GiB is a safe floor consistent with the
# other targets.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
MIN_FREE_KIB="4194304"

# The build command run INSIDE the target container. Two phases:
#
#  1. CONFIGURE (NOT wrapped by Bear - autotools configure probes the toolchain
#     and writes Makefiles; it is not a compile). Fedora installs the Open MPI
#     wrappers under /usr/lib64/openmpi/bin, NOT on the default PATH, so that
#     directory is prepended for the whole command and CC/CXX are set to the
#     bare wrapper names; make then finds them at build time too. CFLAGS carries
#     the determinism self-test hook.
#
#  2. BUILD wrapped by Bear -> Bear's capture at /out/compile_commands.json.
#     Each translation unit is compiled by mpicc (or mpicxx), which execs gcc;
#     Bear must record ONE entry per unit (the wrapper), collapsing the gcc
#     child.
#
# INJECT_CFLAGS is the determinism self-test hook (dogfood-determinism): empty
# on every normal run and on determinism run 1, it carries a perturbing flag on
# determinism run 2 under --inject-fault. It is appended to CFLAGS so it lands
# in the recorded mpicc arguments and the two captures diverge. Empty CFLAGS is
# a harmless no-op on a normal run. /src is fresh each run (a new container), so
# configure re-runs and the flag takes effect.
# shellcheck disable=SC2034
TARGET_BUILD_CMD='mkdir -p /out && export PATH=/usr/lib64/openmpi/bin:$PATH && cd /src && ./configure CC=mpicc CXX=mpicxx CFLAGS="${INJECT_CFLAGS:-}" && ${RPROF_PREFIX:-} bear --output /out/compile_commands.json -- make -j"$(nproc)"'
